### Local environment ###
# Every local env file, whatever the suffix - .env.production and friends carry the same
# secrets as .env and are just as easy to commit by accident. The example is the one
# that must stay tracked, so it is re-included after the wildcard.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.log

# Spring Boot loads ./config/application.yml automatically and at higher precedence
# than the packaged one, which makes it the place for local secrets (SMTP password,
# crypto key). Ignored so those never reach the repository; config/application.yml.example
# is the committed template.
# Pattern note: must be `config/*`, not `config/`. Git does not descend into an excluded
# directory, so a negation under `config/` would never be reached and the template would
# be ignored too.
config/*
!config/*.example
